## 6. Main Backend Components

### 6.1 server.js

`server.js` is the main backend entry point.

Responsibilities include:

* Creating the Express application.
* Loading the PostgreSQL connection.
* Enabling JSON request parsing.
* Registering API routes.
* Providing the health-check endpoint.
* Starting the backend server.

The backend currently runs on:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

---

## 7. Database Connection

The HR360 backend uses the PostgreSQL `pg` package and a connection pool.

The database connection is configured through environment variables.

Configuration parameters include:

```text
DB_HOST
DB_PORT
DB_NAME
DB_USER
DB_PASSWORD
```

The actual database password is stored in `.env` and must not be committed to GitHub.

---

## 8. Environment Configuration

The backend uses `dotenv` to load environment variables.

Example configuration structure:

```text
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=hr360
DB_USER=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=<secured-value>
```

The actual password must never be included in:

* Source code
* Documentation
* Git commits
* GitHub repositories
* Screenshots
* API examples

---

## 9. Express Middleware

The backend currently uses JSON request parsing:

```javascript
app.use(express.json());
```

This allows the API to receive JSON request bodies from clients.

Example:

```json
{
  "employment_status": "RESIGNED"
}
```

---

## 10. API Route Registration

The main server registers the HR360 modules under the `/api` prefix.

Examples:

```text
/api/employees
/api/departments
/api/job-roles
/api/work-statuses
/api/attendance
/api/leave-types
/api/leave-requests
/api/performance-reviews
/api/pips
/api/training-programs
/api/employee-training
/api/interviews
/api/candidates
/api/job-applications
/api/job-offers
/api/analytics
```

This modular routing structure separates functional areas and improves maintainability.

---

