## 22. Architecture Traceability

| Business Area       | Backend Module          | Database Area                                   | API                                                |
| ------------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| Employee Management | Employees               | Employees                                       | `/api/employees`                                   |
| Organization        | Departments / Job Roles | Departments / Job Roles                         | `/api/departments`, `/api/job-roles`               |
| Workforce Status    | Work Statuses           | Work Statuses                                   | `/api/work-statuses`                               |
| Attendance          | Attendance              | Attendance                                      | `/api/attendance`                                  |
| Leave               | Leave                   | Leave Types / Requests                          | `/api/leave-types`, `/api/leave-requests`          |
| Performance         | Performance / PIP       | Reviews / PIPs                                  | `/api/performance-reviews`, `/api/pips`            |
| Training            | Training                | Training / Employee Training                    | `/api/training-programs`, `/api/employee-training` |
| Recruitment         | Recruitment             | Candidates / Applications / Interviews / Offers | Recruitment APIs                                   |
| Analytics           | Analytics               | HR operational data                             | `/api/analytics`                                   |

---

## 23. Non-Functional Considerations

The backend architecture supports:

* Maintainability
* Modularity
* Data integrity
* API consistency
* Configuration security
* Scalability
* Separation of frontend and backend responsibilities
* Future BI integration
* Source-code traceability

